# s2a-ts-install
apps/desktop/src/renderer/main.tsx: in the `try` block of the `if (launchApplication)` branch, right after
  `await Promise.all([remoteShimReady, languageReady]);`
  and before the `if (!remoteBrowser) { void import('./boot-session-read')... }` read and `await import('./bootstrap');`, add
    if (!remoteBrowser) await import('./core-direct/install').then((module) => module.installDirectDesktopApi());
  It is a dynamic import on purpose: install.ts pulls in about 200 renderer modules (i18n, transcript formatting), which must
  not evaluate before the UI language is in place nor ride the first-paint chunk (the order main.tsx's header requires). It is a
  no-op when a preload already supplied window.mixdogDesktop.
apps/desktop/src/preload/index.ts: expose window.mixdogDesktopHost = createHostApi(...) plus the optional `bootContext` and `connection` values (read from the launch arguments as today), and window.mixdogCorePort (installCorePort); stop building the direct members there (the preload-host-api task owns this).
